@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `nii-il34-nouns`
IMPORT `nii-schedule-k1-s369`

-- TESTS for Schedule K1 and s 369(a) (row IL-34). Expected values worked by hand from the Hebrew; the average wage is a round
-- ILLUSTRATIVE 10,000 (an input: s 2(b) average wage, not a published figure), so 5 x = 50,000, 10 x = 100,000, 20 x = 200,000.
--   Days elapsed = end less start. The breach starts 15.1.2026: 14.2.2026 is 30 days (16 to 31 Jan, 14 more); 15.2.2026 is 31.
--   6 months after 15.1.2026 is 15.7.2026; 12 months after is 15.1.2027. "Not exceeding 6 months": the end is not after that day.
--   31.8.2025 + 6 months clamps to 28.2.2026 (the same `add months` the other rows use).

§ `Tests: Schedule K1`

§§ `Fixtures: the readings`

`the readings: event, cash only, no charge when short` MEANS `The readings of Schedule K1` WITH
    `for the period that elapsed` IS `the period runs to the day of the insured event`,
    `for the benefits limb` IS `the limb counts cash benefits only, as Schedule K1 prints`,
    `for a breach of 30 days or less` IS `no charge may be made for a breach of 30 days or less`
`the readings: event, cash and kind, no charge when short` MEANS `The readings of Schedule K1` WITH
    `for the period that elapsed` IS `the period runs to the day of the insured event`,
    `for the benefits limb` IS `the limb counts cash benefits and the money value of benefits in kind, as section 369(a) does`,
    `for a breach of 30 days or less` IS `no charge may be made for a breach of 30 days or less`
`the readings: clearing, cash only, no charge when short` MEANS `The readings of Schedule K1` WITH
    `for the period that elapsed` IS `the period runs to the day the arrears were paid or the employer registered`,
    `for the benefits limb` IS `the limb counts cash benefits only, as Schedule K1 prints`,
    `for a breach of 30 days or less` IS `no charge may be made for a breach of 30 days or less`
`the readings: event, cash only, benefits alone when short` MEANS `The readings of Schedule K1` WITH
    `for the period that elapsed` IS `the period runs to the day of the insured event`,
    `for the benefits limb` IS `the limb counts cash benefits only, as Schedule K1 prints`,
    `for a breach of 30 days or less` IS `a breach of 30 days or less is limited by the benefits limb alone`
`the readings: period declined, cash only, benefits alone when short` MEANS `The readings of Schedule K1` WITH
    `for the period that elapsed` IS `the period that elapsed is declined`,
    `for the benefits limb` IS `the limb counts cash benefits only, as Schedule K1 prints`,
    `for a breach of 30 days or less` IS `a breach of 30 days or less is limited by the benefits limb alone`
`the readings: event, limb declined, no charge when short` MEANS `The readings of Schedule K1` WITH
    `for the period that elapsed` IS `the period runs to the day of the insured event`,
    `for the benefits limb` IS `the benefits limb is declined`,
    `for a breach of 30 days or less` IS `no charge may be made for a breach of 30 days or less`
`the readings: event, cash only, short breach declined` MEANS `The readings of Schedule K1` WITH
    `for the period that elapsed` IS `the period runs to the day of the insured event`,
    `for the benefits limb` IS `the limb counts cash benefits only, as Schedule K1 prints`,
    `for a breach of 30 days or less` IS `a breach of 30 days or less is declined`

§§ `Fixtures: breaches (all start on 15.1.2026)`

`a breach with the event on 1.3.2026 and the arrears paid on 1.3.2026, 30,000 cash` MEANS `An employer's breach, for Schedule K1` WITH
    `the day the payment was due under section 353, or the day the employer should have registered under section 379` IS YMD 2026 1 15,
    `the day of the insured event` IS YMD 2026 3 1, `the day the arrears were paid or the employer registered` IS YMD 2026 3 1,
    `the cash benefits the Institute paid or will pay` IS 30_000, `the money value of the benefits in kind given` IS 0
