§§ `Column A: the rows, both sides of every edge`

#ASSERT `Schedule K1 — the multiple of the average wage for a breach from` (YMD 2026 1 15) `to` (YMD 2026 2 14) `, reading a breach of 30 days or less as` `no charge may be made for a breach of 30 days or less` EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `Schedule K1 — the multiple of the average wage for a breach from` (YMD 2026 1 15) `to` (YMD 2026 2 14) `, reading a breach of 30 days or less as` `a breach of 30 days or less is limited by the benefits limb alone` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT REFUSED `Schedule K1 — the multiple of the average wage for a breach from` (YMD 2026 1 15) `to` (YMD 2026 2 14) `, reading a breach of 30 days or less as` `a breach of 30 days or less is declined` BECAUSE "Schedule K1 has no row for a breach of 30 days or less, and the answer turns on it"
#ASSERT `Schedule K1 — the multiple of the average wage for a breach from` (YMD 2026 1 15) `to` (YMD 2026 2 15) `, reading a breach of 30 days or less as` `a breach of 30 days or less is declined` EQUALS JUST 5
#ASSERT `Schedule K1 — the multiple of the average wage for a breach from` (YMD 2026 1 15) `to` (YMD 2026 7 15) `, reading a breach of 30 days or less as` `a breach of 30 days or less is declined` EQUALS JUST 5
#ASSERT `Schedule K1 — the multiple of the average wage for a breach from` (YMD 2026 1 15) `to` (YMD 2026 7 16) `, reading a breach of 30 days or less as` `a breach of 30 days or less is declined` EQUALS JUST 10
#ASSERT `Schedule K1 — the multiple of the average wage for a breach from` (YMD 2026 1 15) `to` (YMD 2027 1 15) `, reading a breach of 30 days or less as` `a breach of 30 days or less is declined` EQUALS JUST 10
#ASSERT `Schedule K1 — the multiple of the average wage for a breach from` (YMD 2026 1 15) `to` (YMD 2027 1 16) `, reading a breach of 30 days or less as` `a breach of 30 days or less is declined` EQUALS JUST 20
-- Month ends clamp: 31.8.2025 + 6 months is 28.2.2026.
#ASSERT `Schedule K1 — the multiple of the average wage for a breach from` (YMD 2025 8 31) `to` (YMD 2026 2 28) `, reading a breach of 30 days or less as` `a breach of 30 days or less is declined` EQUALS JUST 5
#ASSERT `Schedule K1 — the multiple of the average wage for a breach from` (YMD 2025 8 31) `to` (YMD 2026 3 1) `, reading a breach of 30 days or less as` `a breach of 30 days or less is declined` EQUALS JUST 10
-- 29.2.2024 + 12 months clamps to 28.2.2025.
#ASSERT `Schedule K1 — the multiple of the average wage for a breach from` (YMD 2024 2 29) `to` (YMD 2025 2 28) `, reading a breach of 30 days or less as` `a breach of 30 days or less is declined` EQUALS JUST 10
#ASSERT `Schedule K1 — the multiple of the average wage for a breach from` (YMD 2024 2 29) `to` (YMD 2025 3 1) `, reading a breach of 30 days or less as` `a breach of 30 days or less is declined` EQUALS JUST 20
-- An end before the start.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Schedule K1 — the multiple of the average wage for a breach from` (YMD 2026 1 15) `to` (YMD 2026 1 14) `, reading a breach of 30 days or less as` `a breach of 30 days or less is declined` BECAUSE "the period that elapsed cannot end before it began"

§§ `Column B: the most the clerk may charge, readings chosen`

-- Row 1: 5 x 10,000 = 50,000. Cash 30,000: the lesser of 50,000 and 30,000.
#ASSERT `Schedule K1 — the most the clerk may charge: breach` `a breach with the event on 1.3.2026 and the arrears paid on 1.3.2026, 30,000 cash` `, average wage` 10_000 `, reading Schedule K1 as` `the readings: event, cash only, no charge when short` EQUALS 30_000
-- Row 1, cash 60,000 (kind 5,000): the multiple limb binds at 50,000, cash-only or with kind.
#ASSERT `Schedule K1 — the most the clerk may charge: breach` `a breach with the event on 1.3.2026 and the arrears paid on 1.3.2026, 60,000 cash, 5,000 in kind` `, average wage` 10_000 `, reading Schedule K1 as` `the readings: event, cash only, no charge when short` EQUALS 50_000
#ASSERT `Schedule K1 — the most the clerk may charge: breach` `a breach with the event on 1.3.2026 and the arrears paid on 1.3.2026, 60,000 cash, 5,000 in kind` `, average wage` 10_000 `, reading Schedule K1 as` `the readings: event, cash and kind, no charge when short` EQUALS 50_000
-- Row 2 (the arrears paid on 1.12.2026, 320 days on, over 6 months and under 12): 10 x 10,000 = 100,000. Cash 150,000: 100,000.
#ASSERT `Schedule K1 — the most the clerk may charge: breach` `a breach with the event on 1.3.2026, the arrears paid on 1.12.2026, 150,000 cash` `, average wage` 10_000 `, reading Schedule K1 as` `the readings: clearing, cash only, no charge when short` EQUALS 100_000
-- ... and to the event (1.3.2026, row 1) the same breach is 50,000.
#ASSERT `Schedule K1 — the most the clerk may charge: breach` `a breach with the event on 1.3.2026, the arrears paid on 1.12.2026, 150,000 cash` `, average wage` 10_000 `, reading Schedule K1 as` `the readings: event, cash only, no charge when short` EQUALS 50_000
-- Row 3: 20 x 10,000 = 200,000; cash 300,000.
#ASSERT `Schedule K1 — the most the clerk may charge: breach` `a breach with the event on 1.2.2027, 300,000 cash` `, average wage` 10_000 `, reading Schedule K1 as` `the readings: event, cash only, no charge when short` EQUALS 200_000
-- A short breach: no charge, or the benefits alone (30,000 cash).
#ASSERT `Schedule K1 — the most the clerk may charge: breach` `a short breach, event and arrears paid on 30.1.2026, 30,000 cash` `, average wage` 10_000 `, reading Schedule K1 as` `the readings: event, cash only, no charge when short` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `Schedule K1 — the most the clerk may charge: breach` `a short breach, event and arrears paid on 30.1.2026, 30,000 cash` `, average wage` 10_000 `, reading Schedule K1 as` `the readings: event, cash only, benefits alone when short` EQUALS 30_000

§§ `s 369(a): the most the Institute can charge (cash + kind, up to column B)`

-- Row 1 (50,000), cash 30,000 + kind 5,000. Cash-only limb: column B = min(50,000, 30,000) = 30,000, charge min(35,000, 30,000) = 30,000.
#ASSERT `s 369(a) — the most the Institute can charge the employer: breach` `a breach with the event on 1.3.2026 and the arrears paid on 1.3.2026, 30,000 cash, 5,000 in kind` `, average wage` 10_000 `, reading Schedule K1 as` `the readings: event, cash only, no charge when short` EQUALS 30_000
-- With kind: column B = min(50,000, 35,000) = 35,000, charge min(35,000, 35,000) = 35,000.
#ASSERT `s 369(a) — the most the Institute can charge the employer: breach` `a breach with the event on 1.3.2026 and the arrears paid on 1.3.2026, 30,000 cash, 5,000 in kind` `, average wage` 10_000 `, reading Schedule K1 as` `the readings: event, cash and kind, no charge when short` EQUALS 35_000
-- Cash 48,000 + kind 5,000: cash-only 48,000; with kind min(50,000, 53,000) = 50,000, charge min(53,000, 50,000) = 50,000.
#ASSERT `s 369(a) — the most the Institute can charge the employer: breach` `a breach with the event on 1.3.2026 and the arrears paid on 1.3.2026, 48,000 cash, 5,000 in kind` `, average wage` 10_000 `, reading Schedule K1 as` `the readings: event, cash only, no charge when short` EQUALS 48_000
#ASSERT `s 369(a) — the most the Institute can charge the employer: breach` `a breach with the event on 1.3.2026 and the arrears paid on 1.3.2026, 48,000 cash, 5,000 in kind` `, average wage` 10_000 `, reading Schedule K1 as` `the readings: event, cash and kind, no charge when short` EQUALS 50_000

§§ `The switches (fork K1, K2, K3): answered where the readings agree, declined where they differ`

-- At the switch (all declined): event = arrears paid, no benefits in kind, not short: every reading agrees: 30,000.
#ASSERT `s 369(a) — the most the Institute can charge the employer: breach` `a breach with the event on 1.3.2026 and the arrears paid on 1.3.2026, 30,000 cash` `, average wage` 10_000 EQUALS 30_000
-- K2: kind 5,000 with cash 30,000 below the 50,000 cap: the readings give 30,000 and 35,000: declined.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 369(a) — the most the Institute can charge the employer: breach` `a breach with the event on 1.3.2026 and the arrears paid on 1.3.2026, 30,000 cash, 5,000 in kind` `, average wage` 10_000 BECAUSE "Schedule K1 prints cash benefits only, and section 369(a) charges benefits in kind too, and the answer turns on it"
-- K2: kind 5,000 but cash 60,000 already over the cap: both give 50,000: answered.
#ASSERT `s 369(a) — the most the Institute can charge the employer: breach` `a breach with the event on 1.3.2026 and the arrears paid on 1.3.2026, 60,000 cash, 5,000 in kind` `, average wage` 10_000 EQUALS 50_000
-- K3: a short breach with benefits: no charge (0) or 30,000: declined. With no benefits both are 0: answered.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 369(a) — the most the Institute can charge the employer: breach` `a short breach, event and arrears paid on 30.1.2026, 30,000 cash` `, average wage` 10_000 BECAUSE "Schedule K1 has no row for a breach of 30 days or less, and the answer turns on it"
#ASSERT `s 369(a) — the most the Institute can charge the employer: breach` `a short breach, event and arrears paid on 30.1.2026, no benefits` `, average wage` 10_000 EQUALS 0
-- K1 alone declined (limb cash only, short breach benefits alone): event 30.1.2026 (short) vs arrears paid 1.3.2026 (row 1): with 30,000 cash both give 30,000: answered;
-- with 60,000 cash the event gives 60,000 and the later day gives 50,000: declined.
#ASSERT `s 369(a) — the most the Institute can charge the employer: breach` `a breach with the event on 30.1.2026 and the arrears paid on 1.3.2026, 30,000 cash` `, average wage` 10_000 `, reading Schedule K1 as` `the readings: period declined, cash only, benefits alone when short` EQUALS 30_000
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 369(a) — the most the Institute can charge the employer: breach` `a breach with the event on 30.1.2026 and the arrears paid on 1.3.2026, 60,000 cash` `, average wage` 10_000 `, reading Schedule K1 as` `the readings: period declined, cash only, benefits alone when short` BECAUSE "section 369(a) does not say to what day the period that elapsed runs, and the answer turns on it"
-- The benefits limb declined alone (K1 event, K3 no charge): kind 5,000 under the cap: declined; cash 60,000: answered.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 369(a) — the most the Institute can charge the employer: breach` `a breach with the event on 1.3.2026 and the arrears paid on 1.3.2026, 30,000 cash, 5,000 in kind` `, average wage` 10_000 `, reading Schedule K1 as` `the readings: event, limb declined, no charge when short` BECAUSE "Schedule K1 prints cash benefits only, and section 369(a) charges benefits in kind too, and the answer turns on it"
#ASSERT `s 369(a) — the most the Institute can charge the employer: breach` `a breach with the event on 1.3.2026 and the arrears paid on 1.3.2026, 60,000 cash, 5,000 in kind` `, average wage` 10_000 `, reading Schedule K1 as` `the readings: event, limb declined, no charge when short` EQUALS 50_000
-- K3 declined alone (K1 event, K2 cash only): the short breach with 30,000 cash is declined.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 369(a) — the most the Institute can charge the employer: breach` `a short breach, event and arrears paid on 30.1.2026, 30,000 cash` `, average wage` 10_000 `, reading Schedule K1 as` `the readings: event, cash only, short breach declined` BECAUSE "Schedule K1 has no row for a breach of 30 days or less, and the answer turns on it"
